# DustCriticalMaterials regression test — Phase 23 DOE CM Assessment output.
#
# Tests compute_cm_flux and append_cm_budget with two mine sites.
#
# cm_fractions = 0.001 0.005 0.0
#   bin 0 (d=7 um, PM10): 0.001 kg_CM/kg_dust (0.1% CM by mass)
#   bin 1 (d=2.5 um, PM2.5): 0.005 kg_CM/kg_dust (0.5% CM by mass)
#   bin 2 (d=50 um, coarse): 0.0 (no CM in coarse fraction)
# With transport_bins_separately=false: single bin, cm_fraction[0]=0.001.
#
# Domain: 8x8 cells, 375 m grid. Two sites from Phase 20:
#   mine_north: j=4..7 (32 cells), mine_south: j=0..3 (32 cells).
#
# Critical material flux:
#   F_cm = F_dust * 0.001   [kg_CM/m^2/s]
#   If F_dust ~ 1e-10 kg/m^2/s (typical neutral ABL):
#     F_cm ~ 1e-13 kg_CM/m^2/s per cell
#   Domain total ~ 1e-13 * 64 * (375*375) ~ 9e-7 kg_CM/s
#
# Expected results:
#   (1) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 23 init: cm_fractions=0.001 printed.
#   (2) [DUST DEBUG] advance: cm_flux_max > 0 each step when emission_flux > 0.
#   (3) dust_cm_budget.csv created with header + rows each step.
#       Each step: 1 domain row (site_index=-1) + 3 site rows (0,1,2).
#       After 5 steps: 5*4=20 data rows.
#   (4) dust_cm_budget.csv domain total = site 1 + site 2 + site 0 total.
#   (5) plt_dust_00005 contains 21 variables including dust_cm_flux_kg_CM_m2_s.
#   (6) DustMetadata.json n_variables=21.
#   (7) With cm_fractions empty: [DUST DEBUG] Phase 23 CM tracking disabled.
#       cm_flux_max=0, no dust_cm_budget.csv rows written.
#   (8) Run exits code 0.
#
# To test larger CM fractions: set cm_fractions = 0.1 and verify
# cm_flux_max ~ 0.1 * emission_flux_max.
#
# References:
#   US DOE (2023). Critical Materials Assessment.
#     https://www.energy.gov/eere/vehicles/articles/
#     us-doe-critical-materials-assessment
#   Hofstra et al. (2020). Resources, Conservation and Recycling.
#     https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resconrec.2020.104802
#   USGS Mineral Resources:
#     https://www.usgs.gov/programs/mineral-resources-program
#   Nriagu & Pacyna (1988). Nature, 333, 134.
#     https://doi.org/10.1038/333134a0
#   ERF_FireDiagnostics.H (diagnostic output pattern):
#     https://github.com/hgopalan/ERF/blob/f264ce7dd0f5e727c71c939659a6a5caf001d21b/
#     Source/Fire/ERF_FireDiagnostics.H

